Package: LoopOrder
Type: Package
Title: Tests for Simple Loop Ordered Alternatives in One-Way ANOVA
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Subha", "Halder", email = "sb.halder123456@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements a likelihood ratio test (LoopLRT) and two standardized mean-difference based tests (LoopMax and LoopMin) for testing equality of means against simple loop ordered alternatives in one-way ANOVA. The null hypothesis assumes all group means are equal, while the alternative imposes a loop order structure (H_1: μ_1 ≤ μ_i ≤ μ_k, i=2,3,...k-1) with atleast one strict inequality. Inputs include vectors of sample means, biased variances, and sample sizes along with a significance level; outputs include the test statistic, bootstrap critical value, p-value, and decision.
